{%- comment -%}
  fye-description — the page's meta description, with a LIVE price.

  Added 10/09/2026 (W335). Every product's description_tag metafield was
  generated on 12/08/2026 with that day's price written into the sentence:

      "... and a lifetime warranty. From £2,093."

  Gemex prices move weekly, and a metafield does not, so the text has been
  drifting ever since. Sampled 50 trilogy rings on 10/09: 37 disagreed with
  their own page. Most were out by £11-£80, but three caught by the 19/08
  trilogy restructure were advertising at roughly half price — trl36677-smt
  said "From £862" for a £1,748 ring.

  The fix is to stop storing a price and start computing one. This snippet
  replaces the amount after the final "From £" with the product's live
  price_min, leaving every other word of the copy exactly as written. So the
  sentence stays whatever the copywriter wrote and the number can never go
  stale again, whatever the reprice does.

      {%- capture fye_description -%}
        {%- render 'fye-description', page_type: fye_page_type,
              product: product, description: page_description -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

  Capture it ONCE in layout/theme.liquid and pass it to the meta tag,
  social-meta and schema-product, so the three cannot disagree. That matters
  more than it looks: product.description is empty on most rings (checked
  10/09/2026), so schema-product falls back to this same text, which is how
  the frozen price reached the Product node as well as the snippet.

  WHY ONLY THE NUMBER, and not the wording. The product card says "Setting
  from" on engagement rings, because the centre stone is chosen separately and
  a bare "From" understates by an order of magnitude. These descriptions all
  say "From". Aligning the two is a copy decision and belongs with W206 and
  W166, not smuggled into a bug fix.

  `money_without_trailing_zeros` matches the existing house style: whole
  pounds print as £1,748, and only a real part-pound prints as £2,127.50.

  A description with no "From £" in it, and any non-product page, passes
  through untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign fye_desc = description

  if page_type == 'product' and product != blank and fye_desc contains 'From £'
    assign fye_head = fye_desc | split: 'From £' | first
    assign fye_live = product.price_min | money_without_trailing_zeros
    assign fye_desc = fye_head | append: 'From ' | append: fye_live | append: '.'
  endif

  echo fye_desc | strip
-%}
